# Medusa — read docs first

Before implementing or changing anything related to Medusa (modules, API routes, admin UI, workflows, config), **read the official documentation** and match existing patterns in this repo.

Primary references:
- https://docs.medusajs.com/learn
- Admin UI routes: https://docs.medusajs.com/learn/fundamentals/admin/ui-routes
- Custom modules: https://docs.medusajs.com/learn/fundamentals/modules
- API routes: https://docs.medusajs.com/learn/fundamentals/api-routes
- Medusa JS SDK (admin): https://docs.medusajs.com/resources/js-sdk

Do not guess Medusa-specific APIs, file locations, or bundler behavior. Search docs + this codebase first.

---

# Architecture in this monorepo

| App | Path | Runtime |
|-----|------|---------|
| Backend + Admin | `apps/backend` | Medusa server; **Admin is a Vite SPA (client-only)** |
| Storefront | `apps/storefront` | Next.js App Router (server + client components) |

**Do not confuse Admin (client SPA) with Storefront (Next.js SSR/RSC).** Admin transform/router errors are bundling issues, not SSR mistakes.

---

# `medusa-config.ts` — admin Vite config (critical)

Medusa calls `mergeConfig(baseConfig, customConfig)` for `admin.vite`. **Never spread the incoming config:**

```ts
// WRONG — duplicates @vitejs/plugin-react → esbuild errors:
// "inWebWorker", "prevRefreshReg", "prevRefreshSig" already declared
vite: (config) => ({
  ...config,
  resolve: { ... },
})

// CORRECT — return only the delta; Medusa merges it
vite: () => ({
  resolve: {
    dedupe: ["react", "react-dom", "react-router-dom"],
    alias: {
      "react-router-dom": dashboardReactRouterDom,
    },
  },
}),
```

Reference: https://github.com/medusajs/medusa/issues/11154

When changing `react-router-dom` resolution, resolve the dashboard copy via `createRequire` from `apps/backend/package.json` → `@medusajs/dashboard`, not `process.cwd()` guesses.

